 necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se distribuyen de forma equilibrada entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 84 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 28.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 2.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.2 to 3.8. December accounts for 5% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 14,995 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove misconduct or errors in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to confirm the service type and dates. Review awardee A’s contracts to see if multiple contracts cover the same need. Look for repeated purchases from the same provider to assess if they align with the body’s requirements.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["IvJ21rzS3pg%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","Rcy8nr9ocOLi0Kd8%2Brcp6w%3D%3D","aYamwMgrWjqdkQsA7ROvsg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}